  "id": "circumplex",
  "term": "circumplex",
  "definition": "In psychology, a circumplex is a way of organizing emotional experience within a two-dimensional space. In the circumplex model of affect, feelings are located by their level of pleasure versus displeasure and activation versus deactivation, allowing affective states to be understood as combinations of valence and arousal.",
